    "bomb": {
      "word": "BOMB",
      "definitions": [
        {
          "text": "A great noise; a hollow sound. [Obs.] A pillar of iron . . . which if you had struck, would make . . . a great bomb in the chamber beneath. Bacon.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "(Mil.)",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "A shell; esp. a spherical shell, like those fired from mortars. See Shell.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "A bomb ketch. Bomb chest (Mil.), a chest filled with bombs, or only with gunpowder, placed under ground, to cause destruction by its explosion. strongly built, on which mortars are mounted to be used in naval bombardments; -- called also mortar vessel. whale fishing. noticed volcanic bombs.\" Darwin.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "To bombard. [Obs.] Prior.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "To sound; to boom; to make a humming or buzzing sound. [Obs.] B. Jonson.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        }
      ],
